$$\begin{align*}lw&=450\div10\\lw&=45\text{ mm}^2\end{align*}$$

The whole-number factor pairs of $45$ are $5\times9$, $15\times3$ and $45\times1$. Keeping the height at $10\text{ mm}$ gives:

$5\text{ mm}\times9\text{ mm}\times10\text{ mm}$;

$15\text{ mm}\times3\text{ mm}\times10\text{ mm}$;

$45\text{ mm}\times1\text{ mm}\times10\text{ mm}$.

Each set has volume $450\text{ mm}^3$.
